    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem description\n\nI thought `ensure_languages` would behave like, or even map to `ensure_installed`.\nMeaning I can add languages there, but I can also install via `TSInstall` and it would be loaded automatically.\nBut doing `TSInstall <lang>` is not enough to make them load, because of the autocmd that calls `vim.treesitter.start` for buffers that need it.\n\nI think it would be more clear if it was named something like `enabled_languages`.\nOr a short mention about `vim.treesitter.start` would also suffice. I like that it is not enabled on every buffer though.\n\nEdit: I guess `ensure_installed` has nothing to do whether `vim.treesitter.start` is called or not. So its more that it can be confusing for people who have used `ensure_installed` in a common setup where it would automatically load after `TSInstall`.",
